 ## Background
 
-Phong shading was developed by Bui Tuong Phong in 1975 [S4, unofficial]. It was introduced as a method to generate higher quality images with lighting [S1, S3, unofficial]. It became the de facto baseline for local illumination in computer graphics [S4, unofficial]. The model is based on empirical observations of how light reflects off surfaces, combining ambient, diffuse, and specular components [S2][S7, unofficial].
